# The network of "Connect the branch": the shop's new branch, its line to
# an ISP, the internet beyond, and the shop's cloud network.
#
#   branch --[site]-- r3 ==(wan: the branch's line)== isp ==(core)== r2 --[cloud]-- web
#                                                    1400-byte link
#
# Somewhere on the internet path between the ISP and the cloud, packets of
# at most 1400 bytes get through: isp's core link and r2's wan carry 1400.
# Only the cables are here. Each machine's addresses, routes and tunnel are
# its own settings, in its /etc/network/up; r3's firewall is its
# /etc/nftables.conf, loaded by nftables@r3 once that is enabled.
machine branch
machine r3 router
machine isp router
machine r2 router
machine web

lan site r3:eth0 branch:eth0
link r3:wan isp:line
link isp:core r2:wan
lan cloud r2:lan web:eth0

mtu isp core 1400
mtu r2 wan 1400

run web nginx
